WEBVTT

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:47.870
Rules of the Pretty Boy Detective Club
1. Be pretty. 2. Be a boy. 3. Be a detective.

00:01:49.080 --> 00:02:00.850
It is said that, 'Heaven does not create one person above or below another person.' -From 'An Encouragement of Learning'
by Yukichi Fukuzawa

00:02:00.850 --> 00:02:04.850
LOST ITEM RIGHT IN FRONT OF YOU

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:07.040
H-Hey, wait!

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:08.040
Excuse me!

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:13.590
Oh my, is something the matter?

00:03:13.590 --> 00:03:17.720
U-Um, you dropped th-this.

00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:20.050
Oh no, how could I?

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:25.640
That was quite careless for me to do.

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:29.060
Thank you. You saved me, my boy.

00:03:35.690 --> 00:03:37.820
Hold on! Wait!

00:03:43.870 --> 00:03:44.950
Huh?

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:49.830
ART ROOM, AFTER SCHOOL

00:03:53.380 --> 00:03:55.800
Is something the matter, Dojima?

00:03:55.800 --> 00:04:00.140
Huh? What is it?
You got a request for detective work?

00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:03.560
It's about that bulge
in your breast pocket, isn't it?

00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:09.100
MICHIRU FUKUROI

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:10.060
Whoa.

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:09.850
HYOTA ASHIKAGA

00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:11.350
NAGAHIRO SAKIGUCHI

00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:11.270
My, oh my.

00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:12.850
COUNCILMAN, BOSSMAN, BARE-LEGS

00:04:12.770 --> 00:04:14.270
I see.

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:14.350
PRESIDENT, AND GENIUS

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:16.940
This is quite intriguing!

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:19.410
A man who disappeared into thin air.

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:21.240
It's truly mysterious!

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:25.740
What's the matter, Sosaku?

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:27.870
You look like you want
to say something.

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:40.090
What is it?

00:04:40.090 --> 00:04:44.010
Perhaps this is the first time seeing
a paltry little 10,000 yen bill,

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:45.510
and he finds it unusual?

00:04:50.440 --> 00:04:51.850
I see.

00:04:51.850 --> 00:04:54.060
What's going on, Leader?

00:04:52.390 --> 00:04:54.140
MAYUMI DOJIMA

00:04:54.060 --> 00:05:00.570
Sosaku is merely stating
that this is a counterfeit bill.

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:56.150
MANABU SOTOIN

00:05:00.650 --> 00:05:02.650
CREATION OUT OF HOBBY

00:05:02.870 --> 00:05:05.280
This is counterfeit?

00:05:06.990 --> 00:05:11.540
It has the proper watermarks.
I can't help but think this is real.

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:15.840
That's not how things are,
Mayumi Dojima.

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:18.670
Sosaku is saying the quality is too good.

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:25.930
In other words, they're not getting their
bang for the buck as a counterfeit?

00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:31.270
Such that it's costing more than 10,000
yen to create a 10,000 yen bill?

00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:35.650
That's what this means. Glad you
understood, you have my compliments.

00:05:35.650 --> 00:05:39.530
Spending more than 10,000 yen
to make a 10,000 yen bill...

00:05:39.530 --> 00:05:42.320
What meaning lies
in doing such a thing?

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:44.700
A good question.

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:49.410
Of course, you're able to make a bill that
looks even more real than the real thing.

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:54.000
Looks even more real...

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:55.920
than the real thing...

00:05:55.920 --> 00:06:00.210
So in other words,
it's simply a toy created out of a hobby.

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:02.970
Ridiculous.

00:06:02.970 --> 00:06:05.430
Whether it be
a counterfeit or a real bill,

00:06:05.430 --> 00:06:11.390
it's not something an honest businessman
should be carrying around in his pocket.

00:06:11.390 --> 00:06:15.900
It's not like he shouldn't be doing it,
more like it makes me more cautious

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:18.230
that he's a dangerous man
carrying a wad

00:06:18.230 --> 00:06:22.690
of counterfeit bills
instead of a million yen.

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:24.360
Beautiful!

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:27.780
A counterfeit bill with a budget
surpassing that of the denomination...

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:29.830
That is truly beautiful.

00:06:29.830 --> 00:06:32.370
It has a brilliance that
is simply indescribable.

00:06:32.750 --> 00:06:35.620
I can't quite restrain my curiosity!

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:38.120
BEAUTY SENSOR

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:40.210
In the first place, Dojima,

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:45.760
with your amazing eyesight,
you couldn't tell that this was
a counterfeit bill?

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:49.760
Come to think of it,
this is unlike you, Mayumi the Seer.

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:52.640
Please don't tag me
with nicknames without asking me.

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:55.390
What's this "Mayumi the Seer"?

00:06:55.390 --> 00:06:58.860
I was wearing my glasses at the time,
so it couldn't be helped.

00:06:58.860 --> 00:06:59.940
Glasses?

00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:01.480
Oh, that's right.

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:06.610
You use those glasses to control
your eyesight, which is your beauty.

00:07:06.610 --> 00:07:08.160
Mayumi Dojima.

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:14.500
Let's see here.

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:16.370
Stare.

00:07:17.250 --> 00:07:18.250
Huh?

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:20.410
BILL ENVELOPE

00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:23.880
Stare, stare...

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:30.930
H-Hey, it looks like
there's something inside this bill.

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:34.390
Inside the bill?
What the hell are you talking about?

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:38.850
Michiru.

00:07:38.850 --> 00:07:42.820
Sosaku is saying, "Leave this to me."

00:07:38.930 --> 00:07:40.730
SOSAKU YUBIWA

00:07:55.250 --> 00:07:56.580
Let's see.

00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:01.500
Oh? My, oh my.

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:04.340
Boys, this looks like an invitation.

00:08:06.460 --> 00:08:08.960
INVITATION

00:08:07.090 --> 00:08:08.840
An invitation?

00:08:09.680 --> 00:08:11.470
"Congratulations."

00:08:11.470 --> 00:08:16.890
"You have obtained an entry ticket
to our casino, Reasonable Doubt."

00:08:16.970 --> 00:08:18.970
PLANS FOR SUNDAY

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:19.980
This sounds like a fraud!

00:08:20.270 --> 00:08:22.940
They hold it every Sunday, huh?

00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:24.070
Very well.

00:08:24.070 --> 00:08:25.730
On Sunday night,

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:30.110
we will all gather together and head over
to the venue shown right here.

00:08:30.110 --> 00:08:33.530
Let's see, how do you read these kanji?

00:08:33.530 --> 00:08:39.120
This says "Kamikazari Middle School,
Gymnasium #2," President.

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:37.370
"KAMIKAZARI MIDDLE SCHOOL
GYMNASIUM #2"

00:08:39.670 --> 00:08:41.580
Well, even if counterfeit,

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:46.800
we should go there and return
the 100,000 yen to Mr. Businessman.

00:08:46.800 --> 00:08:50.220
It does say here,
"Please come in plain clothes."

00:08:50.220 --> 00:08:52.760
What kind of clothes are plain clothes?

00:08:52.760 --> 00:08:56.060
I only have shorts
in my personal clothing collection.

00:08:56.060 --> 00:08:58.810
It means dressing up in moderation.

00:08:56.140 --> 00:08:58.890
PLAIN CLOTHES

00:08:58.810 --> 00:09:00.940
Clothing worn on an everyday basis.
Clothing that is not formal."
I see. In moderation, huh?

00:08:58.890 --> 00:09:01.060
PLAIN CLOTHES

00:09:03.190 --> 00:09:06.070
That was a nodding
that got me moderately worried.

00:09:06.150 --> 00:09:08.150
PLAIN CLOTHES IN MODERATION

00:09:16.660 --> 00:09:20.790
Oh, Mayumi Dojima,
you're getting all finished up.

00:09:22.370 --> 00:09:25.090
Thanks to you,
Sosaku looks satisfied!

00:09:25.090 --> 00:09:27.800
What a beautiful exchange
between two team members!

00:09:29.210 --> 00:09:31.880
Okay boys, let us depart!

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:35.350
Time for the Pretty Boy
Detective Club to go to work!

00:09:35.350 --> 00:09:37.350
Just like we always do.

00:09:37.350 --> 00:09:38.600
Tonight, once again, we'll...

00:09:38.600 --> 00:09:39.680
beautifully,

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:41.140
like a boy,

00:09:41.140 --> 00:09:43.810
be detectives!

00:09:43.810 --> 00:09:45.610
--Sure.
--Yes, you're right.

00:09:53.320 --> 00:09:56.700
Each time I see
the perfectly coordinated teamwork,

00:09:56.700 --> 00:10:00.500
I feel like there's no room for me
to squeeze myself in,

00:10:00.500 --> 00:10:04.000
and can't help but feel
a sense of inferiority.

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:11.920
But thanks to an artist, my current self
is a pretty boy, if only on the outside.

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:15.050
I am Mayumi the Seer.

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:20.520
And I'll be a part of this team.

00:10:23.010 --> 00:10:26.520
TERRITORY CASINO HALL 'REASONABLE DOUBT'

00:10:44.420 --> 00:10:47.380
It looked like paradise.

00:10:47.380 --> 00:10:52.460
Everyone is dressed up, but no matter
how you look at them, they were teenagers.

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:55.180
Boys and girls who looked
to be middle-school age.

00:10:57.680 --> 00:10:59.810
Welcome, everyone.

00:10:59.810 --> 00:11:02.930
Pardon me, but do you
have your invitation?

00:11:02.930 --> 00:11:05.190
Oh, yes. Right here.

00:11:06.190 --> 00:11:08.150
Yes, wonderful.

00:11:08.150 --> 00:11:09.940
Thank you very much.

00:11:09.940 --> 00:11:14.860
The chip exchange is to the right of
the stage, so please head there.

00:11:15.900 --> 00:11:18.780
And the cashier is on your left.

00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:20.780
Cashier?

00:11:20.780 --> 00:11:24.660
There's no way a casino
can be child's play.

00:11:24.660 --> 00:11:29.540
Real money is moving here
and not counterfeit bills.

00:11:29.540 --> 00:11:35.260
Now, please enjoy the Reasonable Doubt
Casino to your heart's content.

00:11:35.260 --> 00:11:36.590
Enjoy!

00:11:37.340 --> 00:11:39.340
OPEN THE GAME

00:11:41.600 --> 00:11:43.390
No use just watching.

00:11:43.390 --> 00:11:46.560
Right. Let's just play something.

00:11:46.560 --> 00:11:49.860
Make sure to gather
some information as well, Hyota.

00:11:49.860 --> 00:11:52.150
Please don't lose sight
of our initial objective.

00:11:53.900 --> 00:11:58.410
Now, how to bet.
This is where you show your aestheticism!

00:12:09.830 --> 00:12:13.710
Oh no, Mayumi Dojima,
you'll just be watching.

00:12:14.760 --> 00:12:21.720
No matter what game you play, your vision
would make it cheating, Mayumi the Seer.

00:12:21.720 --> 00:12:24.220
As you can see what's on
the other side of the cards,

00:12:24.220 --> 00:12:27.270
it'll be a problem for you
to bet on money to play in a casino.

00:12:31.060 --> 00:12:37.440
You could say that I don't know the rules
for most of the games in this casino.

00:12:41.530 --> 00:12:42.570
Oh?

00:12:45.490 --> 00:12:48.410
Of all things, he chose blackjack.

00:12:48.410 --> 00:12:53.590
I can't quite speak for him,
but does Sotoin know how to play?

00:12:57.050 --> 00:13:00.220
Now I know poker at least a little bit.

00:13:04.760 --> 00:13:08.730
Well, this might be the easiest game
to understand in a casino.

00:13:11.900 --> 00:13:13.230
Baccarat?

00:13:13.230 --> 00:13:15.980
Um, what kind of a game was it?

00:13:18.900 --> 00:13:20.740
Slot machine, huh?

00:13:20.740 --> 00:13:25.740
He really seems to fundamentally
like playing by himself.

00:13:25.740 --> 00:13:30.290
Well, how do I say it? As long as
I'm watching like this, it's wholesome.

00:13:30.290 --> 00:13:33.960
I don't feel anything corrupt
like taking every last bit

00:13:33.960 --> 00:13:35.630
of allowances from children.

00:13:39.470 --> 00:13:41.430
But it's still illegal, okay?

00:13:42.380 --> 00:13:45.890
Pardon me, but is everything all right?

00:13:46.010 --> 00:13:48.010
MR. BUSINESSMAN, OR RATHER

00:13:52.100 --> 00:13:56.400
It seems you aren't having that much fun.
Is something the matter?

00:13:56.400 --> 00:13:57.650
My dear customer.

00:13:57.650 --> 00:14:03.360
Oh, um, I-I simply
don't know the rules too well,

00:14:03.360 --> 00:14:05.570
and I just tagged along with friends...

00:14:05.570 --> 00:14:08.450
I see. Friends, hm?

00:14:08.450 --> 00:14:11.540
Then I would like to entertain you.

00:14:11.540 --> 00:14:13.580
How about we relive childhood innocence...

00:14:16.250 --> 00:14:18.460
and play some Othello?

00:14:18.460 --> 00:14:20.920
Um, are you...

00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:22.720
Oh, I'm terribly sorry.

00:14:22.720 --> 00:14:29.060
My name is Fudatsuki,
and I am the manager of this casino.

00:14:29.060 --> 00:14:31.310
At the same time,
I am the student council president

00:14:31.310 --> 00:14:34.140
here at Kamikazari Middle School.

00:14:34.140 --> 00:14:35.940
Student council president?

00:14:35.940 --> 00:14:40.360
Then he's no businessman.
He's a middle school student!

00:14:40.360 --> 00:14:44.490
Um, so if you're the student council
president, you're a third-year?

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:44.570
STUDENT
COUNCIL
ADMINISTRATION

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:44.570
PRESIDENT

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:44.570
PRESIDENT

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:44.570
VICE-PRESIDENT

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:44.570
SECRETARY . ACCOUNTING

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:44.570
STANDING COMMITTEE

00:14:44.570 --> 00:14:49.570
STUDENT
COUNCIL
ADMINISTRATION

00:14:44.570 --> 00:14:49.570
PRESIDENT

00:14:44.570 --> 00:14:49.570
PRESIDENT

00:14:44.570 --> 00:14:49.570
VICE-PRESIDENT

00:14:44.570 --> 00:14:49.570
STANDING COMMITTEE

00:14:46.950 --> 00:14:49.700
The change of power
occurs quickly at our school.

00:14:49.700 --> 00:14:51.950
Unlike Yubiwa Academy.

00:14:53.750 --> 00:14:58.670
He knows that I'm a student
at Yubiwa Academy.

00:14:58.670 --> 00:15:03.010
Well, the last time I saw him,
I was wearing my school uniform,

00:15:03.010 --> 00:15:06.090
so it's only natural
that he would know.

00:15:07.050 --> 00:15:09.970
If that's the case,
we need to act very carefully.

00:15:12.100 --> 00:15:14.810
As a member of
the Pretty Boy Detective Club!

00:15:18.610 --> 00:15:21.860
White or black,
please choose your favorite.

00:15:31.370 --> 00:15:35.870
It seems you have
something on your mind?

00:15:35.870 --> 00:15:40.210
I-I was just worried if
it was going to be okay.

00:15:40.210 --> 00:15:43.800
Playing such extravagant games
on school grounds.

00:15:44.760 --> 00:15:47.130
So that was your concern?

00:15:47.130 --> 00:15:50.850
Please rest assured,
there is nothing to worry about.

00:15:50.850 --> 00:15:55.060
Why is it that I have
nothing to worry about?

00:15:55.060 --> 00:16:01.650
May I ask how
you came across this casino?

00:16:01.650 --> 00:16:05.860
We found an invitation
inside a counterfeit bill.

00:16:06.820 --> 00:16:08.950
Do you have other methods as well?

00:16:08.950 --> 00:16:16.160
Yes. In terms of sending out invitations,
we try all sorts of elaborate methods.

00:16:16.160 --> 00:16:22.000
By hook or by crook,
we strive for entertainment.

00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:26.920
A person with such
a playful mind to discover

00:16:26.920 --> 00:16:30.890
our invitations will
never indict this casino.

00:16:30.890 --> 00:16:35.140
Therefore, confidentiality is assured.

00:16:36.310 --> 00:16:41.860
The phrase "playful mind"
had an undefinable persuasion.

00:16:43.020 --> 00:16:45.440
A counterfeit bill is having a
"playful mind."

00:16:45.440 --> 00:16:51.320
That means this casino might also be
the product of someone's "playful mind."

00:16:53.330 --> 00:16:56.290
Has this been profitable?

00:16:56.290 --> 00:17:01.290
Oh my, are you worried
for our well-being?

00:17:01.290 --> 00:17:03.380
Thank you so much.

00:17:03.380 --> 00:17:06.000
We have definitely been making a profit.

00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:10.680
This is not the only enterprise
that I am dabbling in.

00:17:10.680 --> 00:17:14.970
It's just for fun. Entertainment. I guess
you could say it's an investment, too.

00:17:16.140 --> 00:17:18.850
Manager, a problem has arisen.

00:17:18.970 --> 00:17:20.970
ARISEN PROBLEM

00:17:21.230 --> 00:17:22.940
Whoa.

00:17:29.950 --> 00:17:31.860
The student council president...

00:17:31.860 --> 00:17:37.370
Is the student council president of Yubiwa
Academy Middle School one of your friends?

00:17:39.410 --> 00:17:42.370
Of course he'd figure it out.

00:17:42.370 --> 00:17:44.460
Whether or not we're friends aside...

00:17:44.460 --> 00:17:47.880
Um, well, he's my colleague.

00:17:49.420 --> 00:17:54.140
It seems you're worried
about what I'll do with him.

00:17:54.140 --> 00:17:59.850
He will be receiving some
special service.

00:18:00.510 --> 00:18:02.510
EMPTY STAGE

00:18:03.850 --> 00:18:06.940
We have to hand it to the Pretty Boy
Detective Club vice-president.

00:18:06.940 --> 00:18:12.780
He's quite attractive on the stage.
Don't you think so, Mayumi Dojima?

00:18:15.030 --> 00:18:16.910
A "special program."

00:18:17.240 --> 00:18:21.620
Apparently, patrons who win more
than a certain amount of money

00:18:21.620 --> 00:18:26.880
go up on stage and get a chance
to play against the casino manager.

00:18:28.050 --> 00:18:31.920
That competition is
a main event for the casino,

00:18:31.920 --> 00:18:35.050
such that they make
a show of it on the stage.

00:18:35.050 --> 00:18:38.220
Of course, that's also
subject to gambling.

00:18:38.930 --> 00:18:44.520
The manager has never lost
on this special program.

00:18:44.520 --> 00:18:50.320
The rule is that the opponent must place
all chips he has gained on the table.

00:18:51.240 --> 00:18:53.860
If the opponent were victorious,

00:18:53.860 --> 00:19:00.240
what they can gain isn't triple,
or ten times the number of chips they bet.

00:19:00.240 --> 00:19:01.660
It's everything.

00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:08.960
The winner will be given the rights from
the manager to operate this casino.

00:19:08.960 --> 00:19:10.750
Absolute confidence.

00:19:10.750 --> 00:19:14.630
Or should I say absolute "playful mind"?

00:19:14.630 --> 00:19:16.430
Ahem!

00:19:16.430 --> 00:19:21.600
Oh, there's nothing to worry.
Rest assured, Mayumi Dojima!

00:19:21.600 --> 00:19:26.270
He decided to go up on stage on his
own accord. He knows what's going on.

00:19:26.970 --> 00:19:28.980
SPECIAL PROGRAM

00:19:29.150 --> 00:19:31.940
Ladies and gentlemen!

00:19:31.940 --> 00:19:35.320
We will now hold our Special Program
that we haven't had in a while!

00:19:35.320 --> 00:19:37.990
Let's Open The Game!

00:19:45.750 --> 00:19:49.080
Hey, do all of you know about that guy?

00:19:49.080 --> 00:19:51.840
I knew his name, if nothing else.

00:19:51.840 --> 00:19:54.970
The student council president
of Kamikazari Middle School.

00:19:54.970 --> 00:19:58.340
Unlike ours, I heard
he's quite a shrewd guy.

00:19:58.340 --> 00:20:01.760
It's surprising to find out he was doing
something like this behind the scenes.

00:20:04.600 --> 00:20:06.020
Did something happen?

00:20:07.060 --> 00:20:10.610
Looks like Nagahiro
outmaneuvered him out of the blue.

00:20:10.610 --> 00:20:13.280
He set up something that unexpected?

00:20:13.280 --> 00:20:18.820
Who knows? Perhaps I'm being oblivious
because I don't know the rules of poker.

00:20:18.820 --> 00:20:21.120
You don't know, either?

00:20:21.120 --> 00:20:25.910
Unfortunately, I am not learned.
What I have is just aestheticism.

00:20:31.130 --> 00:20:36.470
And the next game, round two,
seemed to favor Sakiguchi as well.

00:20:37.720 --> 00:20:42.350
Apparently Fudatsuki won round three.

00:20:42.350 --> 00:20:44.640
The game count is 2-1,

00:20:44.640 --> 00:20:48.230
but the number of chips has returned
to basically where they started.

00:20:48.230 --> 00:20:51.230
The game continued in a similar manner.

00:20:57.650 --> 00:21:01.410
And then that incident happened.

00:21:01.490 --> 00:21:03.490
STAGEHAND

00:21:04.580 --> 00:21:10.370
I'm the only one who noticed. Only I saw.

00:21:28.310 --> 00:21:31.440
I'm the only one who can see that?

00:22:16.230 --> 00:22:18.320
This is cheating!

00:22:16.310 --> 00:22:21.020
THE SWINDLER, THE VANISHING MAN, AND THE PRETTY BOYS

00:22:16.310 --> 00:22:21.020
(PART 1)
